hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7109","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not give me any answer. My fellow women came to me and I told them: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not give me any answer. So those women said: By Allah, we will not let the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) remain like this (i.e., we will surely speak to him about this). Lady Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Then I spoke to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) about this matter two or perhaps three times, and each time the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent. Then he said: O Umm Salamah! Do not trouble me regarding Aisha. By Allah, among my wives, revelation does not descend upon me in the house of any woman except Aisha. Lady Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I said: I seek refuge with Allah from ever causing you any harm regarding Aisha (i.e., from troubling you)."
"7110","""Aishah said: 'Shall I not tell you about me and about the Prophet?' We said: 'Yes.' She said: 'When it was my night when he was with me' - meaning the Prophet -'He came back (from 'Isha' prayer), put his sandals by his feet and spread the edge of his Izar on his bed. He stayed until he thought that I had gone to sleep. Then he put his sandals on slowly, picked up his cloak slowly, then opened the door slowly and went out slowly. I covered my head, put on my vie and tightened my waist wrapper, then I followed his steps until he came to Al-Baqi'. He raised his hands three times, and stood there for a long time, then he left and I left. He hastened and I also hastened; he ran and I also ran. He came (to the house) and I also came, but I got there first and entered, and as I lay down he came in. He said: ""Tell me, or the Subtle, the All-Aware will tell me.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransomed for you,' and I told him (the whole story). He said: 'So you were the black shape that I saw in front of me?' I said, 'Yes.' He gave me a nudge on the chest which I felt, then he said: 'Did you think that Allah and His Messenger would deal unjustly with you?' I said: 'Whatever the people conceal, Allah knows it.' He said: Jibril came to me when I saw you, but he did not enter upon me because you where not fully dressed. He called me but he concealed that from you, and I answered him, but I concealed that from you too. I thought that you had gone to sleep and I did not want to wake you up, and I was afraid that you would be frightened. He told me to go to Al-Baqi' and pray for forgiveness for them.' I said: 'What should I say, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Say"" Peace be upon the inhabitants of this place among the believers and Muslims. May Allah have mercy upon those who have gone on ahead of us and those who come later on, and we will join you, if Allah wills.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2037)"
"7111","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive Aisha her past and future sins, what she has done secretly and what she has done openly, forgive all of them. Upon this, Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) laughed so much that her head fell into her lap due to laughter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: Does my supplication please you? Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) asked: Why should your supplication not please me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: By Allah, I make this supplication for my Ummah in every prayer."
"7112","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: I can well discern when you are pleased with me and when you are annoyed with me. I said: How do you discern it? Thereupon be said: When you are pleased with me you say;"" No, by the Lord of Muhammad,"" and when you are annoyed with me, you say:"" No, by the Lord of Ibrahim."" I said: Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I in fact leave your name (when I am annoyed with you). (Using translation from Muslim 2439a)"
"7113","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘The superiority of ‘Aishah over other women is like the superiority of Tharid over all other foods.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3281)"
"7114","“Many men have attained perfection but no women have attained perfection except Maryam bint ‘Imran (Mary) and Asiyah the wife of Fir’awn. And the superiority of ‘Aishah over other women is like the superiority of Tharid over all other foods.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3280)"
"7115","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘The superiority of ‘Aishah over other women is like the superiority of Tharid over all other foods.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3281)"
"7116","I realized that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wanted to use it. I took it, cut it, chewed it, and cleaned it, then I offered it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He used the miswak thoroughly; I had never seen him use the miswak in that manner before. Then, as he began to lean towards me, it fell from his hand. I began to recite the same supplication that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite when he was ill, but during this illness, he had not recited that supplication. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his gaze towards the sky and said: (I) choose the Highest Companion. Thus, his soul departed. All praise is due to Allah, who united my saliva and the saliva of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on the last day of his worldly life."
"7117","The Prophet (peace be upon him) put his blessed saliva in his mouth; this was the first thing that entered his mouth. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: This is Abdullah, and you are Umm Abdullah. After that, this remained my title continuously, even though I had no children."
"7118","that the Prophet ﷺ married her when she was six years old and he consummated his marriage when she was nine years old, and then she remained with him for nine years (i.e., till his death). (Using translation from Bukhārī 5133)"
"7119","Abu ʿAbdur-Rahman as-Sulami and Hibban bin ʿAtiyyah had a dispute. ʿAbdur-Rahman said to Hibban: I know what made your companion - meaning ʿAli ؓ - audacious. He said: What is it, may you be bereft of your father? He said. Something I heard ʿAli ؓ say. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, az-Zubair and Abu Marthad on a mission, and we were all horsemen. He said: ʿGo to Rawdat Khakh, for there you will find a woman who has a letter with her from Hatib bin Abi Baltaʿah to the mushrikeen; bring it to me.ʿ So we went on our horses until we caught up with her where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had told us, travelling on a camel of hers. He [Hatib] had written to the people of Makkah, telling them about the march of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We said to her. Where is the letter you have with you? She said: I do not have any letter. We made her camel kneel down and searched her luggage for it, but we did not find anything. My two companions said: We do not see any letter with her, I said: You know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not tell a lie. Then I swore: By the One by whom oaths are sworn, you will give us the letter or we will remove your clothes. She stretched out her hand to her girdle, which was wrapped around her, and brought out the letter. I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and they said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he has betrayed Allah and His Messenger and the believers; let me strike his neck. He said: ʿO Hatib, what made you do what you did?ʿ He said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, by Allah, it is not that I do not believe in Allah and His Messenger, but I wanted to do a favour for the people by means of which Allah might protect my family and my property, for every one of your Companions has some of his people there through whom Allah will protect his family and his property. He said: You have spoken the truth, do not say anything to him but good.ʿ ʻUmar said: O, Messenger of Allah, he betrayed Allah and His Messenger and the believers, let me strike his neck. He said. ʿls he not one of the people of Badr? How do you know? Perhaps Allah looked upon them and said. “Do what you like, for Paradise is guaranteed for you.ʻʼ ʻUmarʻs eyes filled with tears and he said: Allah, may He be exalted, and His Messenger know best. (Using translation from Aḥmad 827)"
"7120","Hatib will definitely go to Hell. (But) Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You tell a lie; he would not get into that for he had taken part in Badr and in (the expedition of) Hudaibiya. (Using translation from Muslim 2495)"
"7121","'Utba b. Ghazwan delivered us a sermon and he praised Allah and lauded Him, then said: Now coming to the point, verily the world has been given the news of its end and that too quite early. Nothing would be left out of it but only water left in the utensil which its owner leaves, and you are going to shift to an abode which knows no end, and you should shift with the good before you, for we have been told that a stone would be thrown at one side of the Hell and it would go down even for seventy years but would not be able to reach its bottom. By Allah, it would be fully packed. Do you find it something strange, and it has been mentioned that there yawns a distance which one would be able to cover in forty years from one end to another of Paradise, and a day would come when it would be fully packed and you must be knowing that I was the seventh amongst seven who had been with Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had nothing to eat but the leaves of the tree until the corners of the mouth were injured. We found a sheet which we tore in two and divided between myself and Sa'd b. Malik. I made the lower garment with halt of it and so did Sa'd make the lower garment with half of it and today there is none amongst us who has not become the governor of a city from amongst the cities (of the Islamic Commonwealth) and I seek refuge with Allah that I should consider myself great whereas I am insignificant in the eye of Allah. Prophethood does not remain for ever and its impact fades with the result that it changes eventually into kingship, and you would soon come to know and experience those rulers who would come after us and see (how far they are from religion). (Using translation from Muslim 2967a)"
"7122","We used to go to Abdullah b. 'Amr and talk to him, Ibn Numair said: One day we made a mention of Abdullah b. Mas'ud, whereupon he said: You have made mention of a person whom I love more than anything else. I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Learn Qur'an from four persons: Ibn Umm 'Abd (i. e. 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud) he started from him-then Mu'adh b. Jabal and Ubayya b. Ka'b, then Salim the ally of Abu Hudhaifa. (Using translation from Muslim 2464a)"
"7123","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: ""If you turn away, Allah will bring another people in your place, and they w"
"7124","Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: My father was a chief (or a government official). I used to go to a school, and there were two boys with me. While returning from the school, they entered a church, and I also went inside with them. The monk said to them: Did I not forbid you both from bringing anyone to me? Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I kept coming to him until I became more beloved to him than those two boys. The monk said to me: O Salman, yo"
"7125","We were sitting in the company of Hudhaifa. A man said: If I were in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would have fought by his side and would have striven hard for his causes. Hudhaifa said: You might have done that, (but you should not make a flourish of your enthusiasm). I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the Battle of Abzib and we were gripped by a violent wind and severe cold. The Messenger of Allah (may peace be him) said: Hark, the man who (goes reconnoitring and) brings me the news of the enemy shall be ranked with me on the Day of Judgment by Allah (the Glorious and Exalted). We all kept quiet and none of us responed to him. (Again) he said: Hark, a man who (goes reconnoitring and) brings me the news of the enemy shall be ranked with me on the Day of Judgment by Allah (the Glorious and Exalted). We kept quiet and none of us responded to him. He again said: Hark, a man who (goes reconnoitring and) brings me the news of the enemy shall be ranked with me on the Day of Judgtuent by Allah (the Glorious and Exalted) Then he said: Get up Hudhaifa, bring me the news of the enemy. When he called me by name I had no alternative but to get up. He said: Go and bring me information about the enemy, and do nothing that may provoke them against me. When I left him, I felt warm as if I were walking in a heated bath untill I reached them. I saw Abu Sufyan warming his back against fire I put an arrow in the middle of the bow. intending to shoot at him, when I recalled the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"" Do not provoke them against me."" Had I shot at him, I would have hit him. But I returned and (felt warm as if) I were walking in a heated bath (hammam). Presenting myself before him, I gave him information about the enemy. When I had done so, I began to feel cold, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrapped me in a blanket that he had in excess to his own requirement and with which he used to cover himself while saying his prayers. So I continued to sleep until it was morning. When it was morning he said: Get up, O heavy sleeper. (Using translation from Muslim 1788)"
"7126","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed voluntary prayers along with those two prayers, then he departed. So I followed behind him. He asked me, ""Who is it?"" I replied, ""Hudhayfah bin Yaman."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Why have you come?"" I informed him about what my mother had said to me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""May Allah forgive you and your mother."
"7127","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him). He asked: How is that? Alqamah replied: I had prayed to Allah Almighty to grant me a righteous companion, so I hope that you are that person. He asked: Who are you? I said: I am from the people of Kufa (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) I am from the people of Iraq and then from the people of Kufa. So Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Are there not among you those special confidants of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) who knew secrets that no one else knew? He meant Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him). Then he asked: Do you remember how Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) used to recite? I replied: Yes. Then he recited (i.e., he recited this Surah) « » Alqamah says: So I recited « » Then Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Him besides whom there is no deity, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also taught me this Surah with these very words from his own tongue, but these people continuously reject what I say. Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: Up to here was the mention of the allies of Quraysh, now after this we will mention the Ansar, among them those who migrated and those who did not migrate (all will be mentioned), if Allah Almighty decrees and wills."
"7128","They made a mention of Ibn Mas'ud before 'Abdullah b. Amr, whereupon he said: He is a person whose love is always fresh in my heart after I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Learn the recita- tion of the Qur'an from four persons: from Ibn Mas'ud, Salim, the ally of Abu Hudhaifa, Ubayy b. Ka'b, Mu'adh b. Jabal. (Using translation from Muslim 2464e)"
"7129","narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""What an excellent man is Abu Bakr, what an excellent man is 'Umar, what an excellent man is Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, what an excellent man is Usaid bin Hudair, what an excellent man is Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, what an excellent man is Mua'dh bin Jabal, and what an excellent man is Mu'adh bin 'Amr bin Al-Jamuh."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3795)"
"7130","Four persons collected the Qur'an during the lifetime of Messenger of Allah ﷺ and all of them were Ansar: Mu'adh b. Jabal, Ubayy b. Ka'b, Zaid b. Thabit, Abu Zaid. Qatada said: Anas, who was Abu Zaid? He said: He was one of my uncles. (Using translation from Muslim 2465a)"
"7131","The Messenger of Allah said: The most merciful of my Ummah towards my Ummah is Abu Bakr; the one who adheres most sternly to the religion of Allah is 'Umar; the most sincere of them in shyness and modesty is 'Uthman; the best judge is 'Ali bin Abu Talib; the best in reciting the Book of Allah is Ubayy bin Ka'b; the most knowledgeable of what is lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh bin Jabal; and the most knowledgeable of the rules of inheritance (Fara'id) is Zaid bin Thabit. And every nation has a trustworthy guardian, and the trustworthy guardian of this Ummah is Abu 'Ubaidah bin Jarrah."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 154)"
"7132","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: The sky has not shaded any person, nor has the earth carried any person, wh"
"7133","We set out from our tribe Ghafir who look upon the prohibited months as permissible months. I and my brother Unais and our mother stayed with our maternal uncle who treated us well. The men of his tribe fell jealous and they said: When you are anay from your house, Unais commits adultery with your wife. Our -naternal uncle came and he accused us of the sin which was conveyed to him. I said: You have undone the good you did to us. We cannot stay with you after this. We came to our camels and loaded (our) luggage. Our maternal uncle began to weep covering himself with (a piece of) cloth. We proceeded on until we encamped by the side of Mecca. Unais cast lot on the camels (we had) and an equal number (above that). They both went to a Kahin and he made Unais win and Unais came with our camels and an equal number along with them. He (Abu Dharr) said: My nephew, I used to observe prayer three years before my meeting with Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: For whom did you say prayer? He said: For Allah. I said: To which direction did you turn your face (for observing prayer)? He said: I used to turn my face as Allah has directed me to turn my face. I used to observe the night prayer at the time of the end of night and I fell down in prostration like the mantle until the sun rose over me. Unais said: I have a work in Mecca, so you better stay here. Unais went until he came to Mecca and he came to me late. I said: What did you do? He said: I met a person in Mecca who is on your religion and he claims that verily it is Allah Who has sent him. I said: What do the people say about him? He said: They say that he is a poet or a Kahin or a magician. Unais who was himself one of the poets said. I have heard the words of a Kahin but his words in no way resemble his (words). And 1 also compared his words to the verses of poets but such words cannot be uttered by any poet. By Allah, he is truthful and they are liars. Then I said: you stay here, until I go, so that I should see him. He said: I came to Mecca and I selected an insignificant person from amongst them and said to him: Where is he whom you call as-Sabi? He pointed out towards me saying: He is Sabi. Thereupon the people of the valley attacked me with sods and bows until I fell down unconscious. I stood up after havin. regained my consciousness and I found as if I was a red idol. I came to Zamzarn and washed blood from me and drank water from it and listen, O son of my brother, I stayed there for thirty nights or days and there was no food for me but the water of Zamzarn. And I became so bulky that there appeared wrinkles upon my stomach, and I did not feel any hunger in my stomach. It was during this time that the people of Mecca slept in the moonlit night and none was there to eircumambulate the House but only two women who had been invoking the name of Isafa, and Na'ila (the two idols). They came to me while in their circuit and I said: Marry one with the other, but they did not dissuade from their invoking. They came to me and I said to them: Insert wood (in the idols' private parts). (I said this to them in such plain words) as I could not express in metaphorical terms. These women went away crying and saying: Had there been one amongst our people (he would have taught a lesson to you for the obscene words used for our idols before us). These women met Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr who had also been coming down the hill. He asked them: What has happened to you? They said: There is Sabi, who has hidden himself between the Ka'ba and its curtain. He said: What did he say to you? They said: He uttered such words before us as we cannot express. Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and he kissed the Black Stone and circumambulated the House along with his Companion and then observed prayer, and when he had finished his prayer, Abu Dharr said: I was the first to greet him with the salutation of peace and uttered (these words) in this way; Allah's Messen- ger, may there be peace upon you, whereupon he said: It may be upon you too and the mercy of Allah. He then said: Who are you? I said: From the tribe of Ghifar. He leaned his hand and placed his finger on his forehead and I said to myself: Perhaps he has not liked it that I belong to the tribe of Ghifar. I attempted to catch hold of his hand but his friend who knew about him more than I dissuaded me f rom doing so. He then lifted his head and said: Since how long have you been here? I said: I have been here for the last thirty nights or days. He said: Who has been feeding you? I said: There has been no food for me but the water of Zamzam. I have grown so bulky that there appear wrinkles upon my stomach and I do not feel any hunger. He said: It is blessed (water) and it also serves as food. Thereupon Abu Bakr said: Messenger of Allah, let me serve as a host to him for tonight, and then Messenger of Allah ﷺ proceeded forth and so did Abu Bakr and I went along with them. Abu Bakr opened the door and then he brought for us the raisins of Ta'if and that was the first food which I ate there. Then I stayed as long as I had to stay. I then came to Allah's Messenaer ﷺ and he said: I have been shown the land abound- ing in trees and I think it cannot be but that of Yathrib (that is the old name of Medina). You are a preacher to your people on my behalf. I hope Allah would benefit them through you and He would reward you. I came to Unais and he said: What have you done? I said: I have done that I have embraced Islam and I have testified (to the prophethood of Messenger of Allah). He said: I have no aversion for your religion and I also embrace Islam and testify (to the prophethood of Muhammad). Then both of us came to our mother and she said: I have no aversion for your religion and I also embrace Islam and testify to the prophethood of Muhammad. We then loaded our camels and came to our tribe Ghifir and half of the tribe embraced Islam and their chief was Aimi' b. Rahada Ghifirl and he was their leader and hall of the tribe said: We will embrace Islam when Messenger of Allah (may p,. ace be upon him) would come to Medina, and when Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Medina the remaining half also embraced Islam. Then a tribe Aslam came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Messenger of Allah, we also embrace Islam like our brothers who have embraced Islam. And they also embraced Islam. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah granted pardon to the tribe of Ghifar and Allah saved (from destruction) the tribe of Aslam. (Using translation from Muslim 2473a)"
"7134","The statement of Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him): ""I was the fourth person to accept Islam,"" means that he was the fourth person from his tribe to accept Islam, because at that time, many people from the Quraysh and other tribes had already become Muslim."
"7135","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: The earth has not carried anyone, nor has the sky shaded anyone, more truthful and more fulfilling of promises than Abu Dharr al-Ghifari. He resembles Sayyiduna Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon him). The narrator states: Sayyiduna Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, should we introduce him in this manner? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes, you should introduce him in this way."
"7136","I replied: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then learn it, letters from (non-Muslim rulers) come to us. Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I learned this language in seventeen days. The narrator named A’mash states: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) wished that only a trustworthy person should be informed of the contents of the letters that came to him."
"7137","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr, and the most severe of them concerning the order of Allah is 'Umar, and the most truly modest of them is 'Uthman bin 'Affan. The best reciter (of the Qur'an) among them is Ubayy bin Ka'b, the most knowledgeable of them concerning (the laws of) inheritance is Zaid bin Thabit, the most knowledgeable of them concerning the lawful and the unlawful is Mu'adh bin Jabal. Truly, every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3791)"
"7138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: To a virgin or to a previously married woman? I replied: To a previously married woman. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Why did you not marry a young girl so that you could play with her and she could play with you, you could make her laugh and she could make you laugh? I replied: (My father) Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away and left behind nine (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps the words are:) seven daughters, and I did not like to bring a wife of their age among them, so I married a woman who would look after them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: May Allah bless you."
"7139","""My father died owing debts. I offered to his creditors that they could take the fruits in lieu of what he owed them, but they refused as they thought that it would not cover the debt. I went to the Messenger of Allah and told him about that, he said: 'When you pick the dates and have put them in the Mirbad (place for drying dates), call me.' When I had picked the dates and put them in the Mirbad, I went to the Messenger of Allah and he came, accompanied by Abu Bakr and 'Umar. He sat on (the dates) and prayed for blessing. Then he said: 'Call your creditors and pay them off.' I did not leave anyone to whom my father owed anything but I paid him off, and I had thirteen Wasqs left over. I mentioned that to him and he smiled and said: 'Go to Abu Bakr and 'Umar and tell them about that.' So I went to Abu Bakr and 'Umar and told them about that, and they said: 'We knew, when the Messenger of Allah did what he did, that this would happen.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3640)"
"7140","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck it with something that he had with him, after which it began to move ahead of the people, to the extent that I had to restrain it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you sell this (camel) to me for such and such amount? May Allah forgive you. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I said, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it is already yours. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you sell it to me for such and such amount? May Allah forgive you. I said, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it is yours."
"7141","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you sell it to me (on this condition) that when we reach Madinah, if Allah wills, I will pay you two dinars. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I said, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this is your camel. After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept repeating this until he fixed the price at 20 dinars, and every time he said, May Allah forgive you. When we reached Madinah and I brought the camel to your service, I said, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this is your camel. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bilal, give him 20 dinars from the spoils of war, and (he said to me) take your camel back to your home."
"7142","narrates: On the night of the incident with the camel, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicated for my forgiveness 25 times."
"7143","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I participated in a battle with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). My camel was walking slowly and it had become tired. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and said: O Jabir! I replied: Yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with you? I replied: My camel is walking slowly and it has become tired, so I am falling behind. Then I got down from the camel. The"
"7144","Verily Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, has commanded me to recite the Qur'an to you, whereupon he said: (Has) Allah mentioned my name to you? He said: Allah has mentioned your name to me. Thereupon he began to shed tears (of joy) (Using translation from Muslim 799d)"
"7145","I will separate you from them just as a hair is taken out from kneaded dough."
"7146","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him): Indeed, the Holy Spirit is with you as long as you satirize them."
"7147","The Holy Spirit will continue to support you as long as you keep responding on behalf of Allah and His Messenger."
"7148","I adjure you by Allah if you had not heard Allah's Apostle ﷺ saying: Hassin, give a reply on behalf of the Messenger of Allah. O Allah, help him with Ruh-ul-Qudus. Abu Huraira said: Yes, it is so. (Using translation from Muslim 2485c)"
"7153","People say that Abu Huraira transmits so many ahadith, whereas Allah is the Reckoner, and they say: How is it with Muhajirs and the Ansar that they do not narrate ahadith like him (like Abu Huraira)? Abu Huraira said: I tell you that my brothers from Ansar remained busy with their lands and my brothers Muhajirs were busy in transactions in the bazars, but I always kept myself attached to Messenger of Allah ﷺ with bare subsistence. I remained present (in the company of the Holy Prophet), whereas they had been absent. I retained in my mind (what the Prophet said), whereas they forgot it. One day Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who amongst you spreads the cloth and listens to my talk and would then press it against his chest would never forget anything heard from me. So I spread my mantle and when he had concluded his talk I then pressed it against my chest and so I never forgot after that day anything that he (the Holy Prophet) said. And if these two verses would not have been revealed in the Book I would have never transmitted anything (to anybody):"" Those who conceal the clear evidence and the guidance that We revealed"" (ii. 159) tip to the last verse. (Using translation from Muslim 2492c)"
"7154","I invited my mother, who was a polytlieist, to Islam. I invited her one day and she said to me something about Messenger of Allah ﷺ which I hated. I came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping and said: Messenger of Allah, I invited my mother to Islam but she did not accept (my invitation). I invited her today but she said to me something which I did not like. (Kindly) supplicate Allah that He may set the mother of Abu Huraira right. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Allah, set the mother of Abu Huraira on the right path. I came out quite pleased with the supplication of Allah's Apostle ﷺ and when I came near the door it was closed from within. My mother heard the noise of my footsteps and she said: Abu Huraira, just wait. And I heard the noise of falling of water. She took a bath and put on the shirt and quickly covered her head with a headdress and opened the door and then said: Abu Huraira, I bear witness to the fact that there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is His bondsman and His Messenger. He (Abu Huraira) said: I went back to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and (this time) I was shedding the tears of joy. I said: Messenger of Allah, be happy, for Allah has responded to your supplication and He has set on the right path the mother of Abu Huraira. He (the Holy Prophet) praised Allah, and extolled Him and uttered good words. I said: Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah so that He may instill love of mine and that of my mother too in the believing servants and let our hearts be filled with their love, whereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Allah, let there be love of these servants of yours, i.e. Abu Huraira and his mother, in the hearts of the believing servants and let their hearts be filled with the love of the believing servants. (Abu Huraira said: This prayer) was so well granted by Allah that no believer was ever born who heard of me and who saw me but did not love me. (Using translation from Muslim 2491)"
"7155","narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to show boldness in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would ask you about things regarding which we would not ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7156","I came to Madinah Munawwarah, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was in Khaybar at that time. A man from the tribe of Banu Ghifar was leading the people in the morning prayer. In the first rak'ah, he recited Surah Maryam, and in the second rak'ah, he recited Surah Mutaffifin. Among us, there was a man who had two types of measures: one was a large measure and the other was a small one. He would give (goods) by measuring with one and receive (goods) by measuring with the other. (This thought came to my mind), so I said: That person is ruined."
"7157","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many clusters of dates have been presented for Abu Dahdah in Paradise!"
"7158","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the funeral prayer of Sayyiduna Abu Dardaah. We were present there at that time. A horse was brought for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he mounted it. He made it run fast, so we began to run around him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: How many clusters of (fruits) have been hung for Abu Dardaah in Paradise."
"7159","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Give it to him in exchange for a date palm tree in Paradise. He did not accept this. Then Abu Dahdah went to him and said: Sell me your date palm tree in exchange for my garden. He agreed to this. Then Sayyiduna Abu Dahdah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I have bought that date palm tree in exchange for my garden, and I dedicate it to you; please give it to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: How many clusters of dates are there for Abu Dahdah in Paradise! He said this several times. Then Abu Dahdah went to his wife and said: O Umm Dahdah, leave the garden, for I have sold it in exchange for a tree in Paradise. The woman said: This is a profitable deal."
"7160","I have received information that the son of Sufyan bin Nubaiah Hudhali has gathered people against me so that they may fight me. At this time (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words:) he is present near the date-palm tree or near ‘Uraynah. Go to him. The narrator says: I submitted: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), please describe his appearance to me so that I may recognize him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The special sign between you and him is that when you see him, you will be overcome with trembling. The narrator says: I drew my sword and set out, until when I reached him, he was at his encampment with his women. This was at the time of ‘Asr. When I saw him, I felt exactly what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had described to me, and I was overtaken by trembling. I moved towards him, but then I feared that the fight between me and him might distract me from prayer, so I performed the prayer, even as I was walking towards him, signaling with my head. When I reached him, he asked: Who is it? I said: I am an Arab. I said: I have heard about you that you have gathered people against that person, so I have come here for that reason. The narrator says: He said: That is indeed my purpose. Then I walked with him for a while, until when I found the opportunity, I struck him with my sword and killed him. Then I left, and his women were bent over him. When I presented myself before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he saw me, he said: This face has succeeded. I submitted: I have killed him, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have spoken the truth. The narrator says: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with me, took me with him into his house, and gave me a staff. He said: O Abdullah bin Anis, keep this staff with you. The narrator says: I took it to the people, and they asked: Whose staff is this? I said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has given it to me, and he has instructed me to keep it safe. The people said: Will you not go back to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him why this is so? The narrator says: I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and submitted: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), why have you given me this staff? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This will be a special sign between me and you on the Day of Resurrection. On that day, very few people will be leaning on something. (The narrator says) So Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) kept it with his sword, and it remained with him continuously, until when he passed away, by his instruction, that staff was placed with him in his shroud and both were buried together."
"7161","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) on"
"7162","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out and I was with him, until he entered the synagogue of the Jews in Madinah Munaw"
"7163","I have never heard the Prophet ﷺ saying about anybody walking on the earth that he is from the people of Paradise except ʿAbdullah bin Salam. The following Verse was revealed concerning him: ""And a witness from the children of Israel testifies that this Qur'an is true"" (46.10) (Using translation from Bukhārī 3812)"
"7164","I had left my brother Umair making ablution, so I thought it would be my brother, but Abdullah bin Salam came and he ate that food."
"7165","I heard the Prophet say this: ""He is the tenth among those ten men who are destined for Paradise."
"7166","I was sitting in a circle in the mosque of Medina and there was an old man, quite handsome. He was 'Abdullah b. Salim. He was telling good things to them (to the people sitting in that company). As he stood up (to depart) the people said: He who is desirous of looking at a person from amongst the people of Paradise should see him. I said: By Allah, I will follow him, and would try to know his residence. So I followed him and he walked on until he reached the outskirts of Medina. He then entered his house. I sought permission from him to get in, and he granted me the permission, saying: My nephew, what is the need (that has brought you here)? I said to him: As you stood up, I heard people say about you: He who is desirous of seeing a person from among the people of Paradise should look at him. So I became desirous of accompanying you. He ('Abdullah b. Salim) said: It is Allah Who knows best about the people of Paradise. I would, however, narrate to you as to why they said like it. (The story is) that while I was asleep (one night) there came to me a person (in the dream) who asked me to stand up. (So I stood up) and he caught hold of my hand and I walked along with him, and, lo, I found some paths on my left and I was about to set out upon them. Thereupon he said to me Do not set yourself on (them) for these are the paths of the leftists (denizens of Hell-fire). Then there were paths leading to the right side, whereupon he said: Set yourself on these paths. We came across a hill and he said to me: Climb up, and I attempted to climb up that I fell upon my buttocks. I made several attempts (but failed to succeed). He led until he came to a pillar (so high) that its upper end touched the sky and its base was in the earth. And there was a handhold at its upper end. He said to me Climb over it. I said: How can I climb upon it, as its upper end touches the sky? He cought hold of my hand and pushed me up and I found myself suspended with the handhold. He then struck the pillar and it fell down, but I remained attached to that handhold until it was morning (and the dream was thus over). I came to Allah's Apostle ﷺ and narrated it to him. He said: So far as the paths which you saw on your left are concerned, these are paths of the leftists (denizens of Hell) and the paths which you saw on your right, these are the paths of the rightists (the dwellers of Paradise) and the mountain represents the destination of the martyrs which you would not be able to attain. The pillar implies the pillar of Islam. and so far as the handhold is concerned, it implies the handhold of Islam, and you would hold to it fastly until you would meet death. (Using translation from Muslim 2484c)"
"7167","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, “Why is that?” He replied, “Allah Almighty has forbidden us from liking something we have not done and being praised for it, and I find within myself that I like to be praised. Likewise, Allah has forbidden us from arrogance, and I find within myself that I like beauty. Allah Almighty has also forbidden us from raising our voices above your voice, and I am a person whose voice is loud.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “O Thabit, are you not pleased that you will live a praiseworthy life, be martyred, and enter Paradise?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).” The narrator states: So he lived a praiseworthy life and was martyred on the day of the battle against Musaylimah the Liar."",""He said: So he lived praiseworthy"",""and he was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylimah the Liar."""
"7168","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) found him absent (and inquired about him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was informed about his situation. He said: (No), rather he is among the people of Paradise. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When we used to see him walking among us, we knew that he was a person of Paradise, but when the Battle of Yamama came, then the situation became clear. He put on his clothes, applied perfume, advanced, participated in the battle, and was martyred."
"7169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) noticed his absence and inquired about him. He was informed: O Messenger of Allah! He says that I fear I may become among the people of Hell because my voice becomes loud in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: (No), rather he is among the people of Paradise. (Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates) So we used to see him walking among us as a person of Paradise."
"7170","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed for beauty for him."
"7171","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed his hand over his face and prayed for his beauty."
"7172","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was looking at me. He said: O Allah, grant him beauty. The narrator says: I saw him at the age of 93, and even then there was not a single white hair on his head or beard."
"7173","The narrator says: The polytheists turned their backs and fled. I descended from the mountain and came before Akhram. I said, “O Akhram, try to avoid them, for I fear they may harm you. Wait until the Prophet () and his companions arrive.” Akhram said, “O Salamah, if you believe in Allah and the Last Day, and know that Paradise is true and Hell is true, then do not stand between me and martyrdom.” The narrator says: So Sayyiduna Salamah let go of his horse’s reins. He reached ‘Abdur Rahman bin ‘Uyainah. ‘Abdur Rahman attacked him; their spears clashed. Akhram cut the legs of ‘Abdur Rahman’s animal, and ‘Abdur Rahman wounded and martyred him. Then ‘Abdur Rahman mounted Akhram’s horse. Then Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah reached ‘Abdur Rahman. Their spears clashed. He cut the legs of Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah’s animal, so Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah killed him. Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah returned riding Akhram’s horse. Then I continued following those people until I could no longer see anything of the Prophet ()’s companions in the dust, while the enemy reached a valley with water just before sunset. That place was called Dhu Qarad. They intended to drink water there. When they saw me coming after them, they left that place and went to the valley of Dhi Sabeel. Meanwhile, the sun set. I came to a man and shot him with an arrow. I said, “Take it! I am the son of Akwa’, and today is the day of the destruction of the lowly ones.” He said, “May my mother weep for me, is it Akwa’ of the morning?” I said, “Yes, O enemy of your own soul.” He was the same person whom I had shot with an arrow in the morning. I shot him with a second arrow, so he was struck by two arrows, and he let go of two horses. I drove both of them and brought them to the Prophet (). The Prophet () was at that time at the water of Dhu Qarad. The Prophet () was with some companions. Sayyiduna Bilal was there, who had slaughtered one of the camels I had left behind. He was roasting its liver and thigh for the Prophet (). I said, “O Messenger of Allah (), grant me permission to select one hundred men from your companions and then attack the disbelievers. I will not leave any informer among them except that I will kill him.” The Prophet () said, “O Salamah, have you done this?” I said, “Yes, by the One who honored your face.” The Prophet () smiled until I could see the teeth at the sides of your mouth in the light of the fire. The Prophet () said, “Those people must have reached the land of Ghatafan by now.” Then a man from Ghatafan came and informed that those people had camped at such-and-such Ghatafani’s place. He had slaughtered a camel for them. While they were skinning it, they saw dust, so they left it and fled. The next morning, the Prophet () said, “The best of our horsemen today is Abu Qatadah, and the best of our foot soldiers today is Salamah.” Then the Prophet () gave me the share of both a foot soldier and a horseman. The Prophet () made me ride behind him on his she-camel ‘Adhba’, and we returned to Madinah Munawwarah. When we were some distance from Madinah Munawwarah, one of the attendees, who was from the Ansar and whom no one could beat in a race, began to call out loudly, “Is there anyone to compete? Will anyone race to Madinah Munawwarah?” He announced this several times. At that time, I was behind the Prophet (). I said, “O Messenger of Allah (), may my parents be sacrificed for you, allow me to compete with this man.” The Prophet () said, “If you wish (then do so).” I said to the Ansari, “Come on (I will compete with you).” He dismounted his mount, I bent my leg and got down from the she-camel, then I let him get ahead to one or two hills (with full force I ran) and caught up with him. I struck him between his shoulders with my hand and said, “By Allah, you have lost,” until we reached Madinah Munawwarah."
"7174","Sayyiduna "",""mainEntityOfPage"":{""@type"":""WebPage"",""@id"":""https://en.tohed.com/hadith/sahih-ibn-hibban/7174/""},""inLanguage"":""en"",""isPartOf"":{""@type"":""CreativeWorkSeries"",""name"":""Hadith Collections""},""articleSection"":""Ibn Hibban"",""about"":[""Book of the Prophet’s ﷺ Reports on the Virtues of the Companions, Men and Women, by Name""],""image"":[""https://en.tohed.com/hadith/assets/og/sahih-ibn-hibban.jpg""],""author"":{""@type"":""Organization"",""name"":""Tohed""},""publisher"":{""@type"":""Organization"",""name"":""Tohed"",""logo"":{"
"7175","The Prophet (peace be upon"
"7176","I participated in fifteen battles along with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). I and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) (both of us participated)."
"7177","My mother Umm Anas came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ. And she prepared my lower garment out of the half of her headdress and (with the other half) she covered my upper body and said: Messenger of Allah, here is my son Unais; I have brought him to you for serving you. Invoke blessings of Allah upon him. Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: O Allah, make an increase in his wealth, and progeny. Anas said: By Allah, my fortune is huge and my children, and grand-children are now more than one hundred. (Using translation from Muslim 2481b)"
"7178","from Umm Sulaim, that she said: ""O Messenger of Allah, Anas bin Malik is your servant, supplicate to Allah for him."" He said: ""O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, and bless him in what You have given him."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3829)"
"7179","The narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words:) If it is decreed, it will happen."
"7180","I was also among those who were overtaken by drowsiness that day. My sword would fall from my hand and I would pick it up, then it would fall again and I would pick it up again. While the other group was that of the hypocrites; they were only concerned about themselves. These people were the most cowardly and the most disgraced. They would have unjust thoughts about Allah, the same thoughts as in the days of ignorance. These were the people who doubted and were suspicious about Allah’s command."
"7181","I will remain in front of you."
"7182","Abu Talha was the one among the Ansar of Medina who possessed the largest property and among his property he valued most was his garden known as Bairaha' which was opposite the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ often visited it and he drank of its sweet water. When this verse was revealed: ""You will never attain righteousness till you give freely of what you love"" (iii. 91), Abu Talha got up and, going to Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: Allah says in His Book: ""You will never attain righteousness till you give freely of what you love,"" and the dearest of my property is Bairaha' so I give it as Sadaqa to God from Whom I hope for reward for it and the treasure with Allah; so spend it, Messenger of Allah, on whatever purpose you deem it proper. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Well done! that is a profitable deal, that is a profitable deal. I have heard what you have said, but I think you should spend it on your nearest relatives. So Abu Talha distributed it among the nearest relatives and his cousins on his father's side. (Using translation from Muslim 998a)"
"7183","""When this Verse was revealed -'By no means shall you attain Al Birr (piety, righteousness--here it means Allah's reward, i.e. Paradise), unless you spend (in Allah's cause) of that which you love'- Abu Talha said: 'Our Lord will ask us about our wealth. I adjure you, O Messenger of Allah! I am giving my land to Allah.' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Make it for your relatives, Hassan bin Thabit and Ubayy bin Ka'b.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3602)"
"7184","I not see that my Lord has commanded me to go forth, whether I am young or old? Prepare my equipment for me. His sons said to him: You participated in battles with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) until the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, then you took part in battles with Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) until he too passed away, then you participated in battle with Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). Now we will go to participate in battle in your place. But Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Prepare my equipment for me. They prepared his equipment, and he set out on a sea journey. During this journey, he passed away. His companions could not find any island to bury him. After seven days of his passing, they found an island (where they could bury him), but during this time, his (body) had not changed at all (i.e., the body had not decayed)."
"7185","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umm Sulaym! Allah has sufficed and brought about a good (outcome)."
"7186","I am fasting."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) went to a corner of the house and performed voluntary prayer there. He called Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) and the members of her household. Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have a special request."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: ""What is it?"" She said: ""Your humble servant Anas (please pray for him)."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: So the Prophet (peace be upon him) prayed for every good for me in this world and the Hereafter, and then he said: ""O Allah! Grant him wealth and children and bless him in them."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: In terms of wealth (i.e., land), I was the wealthiest among the Ansar. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) also mentioned that my daughter Amina has told me that before Hajjaj came to Basra, more than one hundred and twenty people from among my children and grandchildren had passed away."
"7187","The next day, he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in the morning and informed him about the incident of Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her), that is, what she had done. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah bless both of you in the night you spent together."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) became pregnant from that night. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him): ""When Umm Sulaym gives birth to the child, bring him to me."" So Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) brought the child wrapped in a cloth to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) chewed a date and put it in the child's mouth, so the child began to suck it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him): ""The Ansar truly love dates."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed tahneek for the child, named him, and prayed for him. He named him Abdullah."
"7188","I will inform him myself. Then Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) came home tired; he was fasting. Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) applied fragrance for him and got ready for him, and she brought food. Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: How is Abu Umair? Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) said: He has finished his evening meal. Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) ate, and after that, he had relations with his wife. Then Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Abu Talhah, what do you think, if a family lends something to another family, and then the owners of that thing demand it back, should the other people return it or keep it? Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Rather, they should return it to them. So Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Hope for reward from Allah regarding Abu Umair. Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) became angry and went to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him about what Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) had said. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: May Allah bless you both in your night together. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: So Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) became pregnant with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him). When she gave birth to the child, on the seventh day after his birth, Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) said to me: O Anas, take this child and this container in which there are some Ajwa dates, and take them to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) so that he may perform tahneek for the child and suggest a name for him. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I took him to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting with his legs outstretched. He laid the child in his lap, took a date, chewed it, and then put it in the child's mouth. The child began to suck on it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The Ansar truly love dates."
"7189","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and took a nap in our house, then he woke up smiling. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransomed for you, what has made you smile?' He said: 'I saw some people of my Ummah riding on the sea like kings on thrones.' I said: 'Pray to Allah to make me one of them.' He said: 'You will be one of them.' Then he slept again, and woke up smiling. I asked him and he said the same thing. I said: 'Pray to Allah to make me one of them.' He said: 'You will be one of the first.' Then 'Ubadah bin As-Samit married her, and he traveled by sea, and she traveled with him, but when she came ashore a mule was brought to her and she mounted it, and it threw her off and broke her neck."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3172)"
"7190","I entered Paradise and I heard a sound. I asked: Who is this? The angels replied: This is Rumaysa bint Milhan. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Up to here was the mention of the Ansar. Now we will mention (those Companions) who belonged to the Arab tribes after them, who are not counted among the Muhajirun from the Quraysh or the Ansar, if Allah Almighty makes this matter easy and facilitates it."
"7191","I attacked Ibn Duraid and killed him, and I took the flag. Then I, along with the people, presented myself before the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). When he saw me and saw the flag in my hand, he inquired: O Abu Musa! Has Abu Amir been martyred? I replied: Yes, O Messenger of Allah! So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) raised both his hands and prayed for him. He made this supplication: ""O Allah! Include Abu Amir among those who will have the greatest reward on the Day of Resurrection."
"7192","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Some people will come whose hearts will be extremely soft. (The narrator says) Then the people of the Ash‘ari tribe arrived, among whom was Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash‘ari (may Allah be pleased with him). Those people were coming while reciting this rajaz and saying: ""Tomorrow we will meet our beloved ones, we will meet Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and his group."
"7193","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Some people will come to you whose hearts will be extremely soft. Then the people of the Ash‘ari tribe arrived, among whom was Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash‘ari (may Allah be pleased with him). These were the first people who initiated handshaking (musafaha) in Islam. When these people reached near Madinah Munawwarah, they were reciting rajaz poetry and saying: ""Tomorrow we will meet our beloved ones, that is, Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions."
"7194","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to say, ""The people have made one migration, but you have made two migrations."
"7195","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard the recitation of Abu Musa and said: He has been given a Mizmar among the Mazamir of the family of Dawud, peace be upon him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1019)"
"7196","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard the recitation of Abu Musa and said: He has been given a Mizmar among the Mazamir of the family of Dawud, peace be upon him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1019)"
"7197","I heard your recitation; you have been given a melodious voice like the family of Dawud. I said: O Messenger of Allah! If I had known of your presence, I would have recited even more beautifully."
"7198","He (the Holy Prophet) sent me along with Abu 'Amir and Abu 'Amir received a wound in his knee from the arrow, (shot by) a person of Bani Jusham. It stuck in his knee. I went to him and said: Uncle, who shot an arrow upon you? Abu 'Amir pointed out to Abu Musa and said: Verily that one who shot an arrow upon me in fact killed me. Abu Musa said: I followed him with the determination to kill him and overtook him and when he saw me he turned upon his heels. I followed him and I said to him: Don't you feel ashamed (that you run), aren't you an Arab? Why don't you stop? He stopped and I had an encounter with him and we exchanged the strokes of (swords). I struck him with the sword and killed him. Then I came back to Abu Amir and said: Verily Allah has killed the one who killed you. And he said: Now draw out this arrow. I drew out the arrow and there came out from that (wound) water. Abu 'Amir said: My nephew, go to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and convey my greetings to him and tell him that Abu Amir begs you to ask forgiveness for him. And Abu Amir appointed me as the chief of the people and he died after a short time. When I came to Allah's Apostle ﷺ I visited him and he had been lying on the cot woven by strings and there was (no) bed over it and so there had been marks of the strings on the back of Messenger of Allah ﷺ and on his sides. I narrated to him what had happened to us and narrated to him about Abu Amir and said to him that he had made a request to the effect that forgiveness should be sought for him (from Allah). Thereupon Messenger of Allah (may peace be. upon him) called for water and performed ablution with it. He then lifted his hands and said. O Allah, grant pardon to Thy servant Abu Amir. (The Prophet had raised his hands so high for supplication) that I saw the whiteness of his armpits. He again said: O Allah, grant him distinction amongst the majority of Thine created beings or from amongst the people. I said: Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me too. Thereupon Allah's Apostle ﷺ said: Allah, forgive the sins of Abdullah b. Qais (Abu Musa Ash'ari) and admit him to an elevated place on the Day of Resurrection. Abu Burda said: One prayer is for abu 'Amir and the other is tor Abu Musa. (Using translation from Muslim 2498)"
"7199","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greeted me with salam. The people began to look at me attentively. I asked the person sitting next to me: O servant of Allah! Has the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned anything about me? He replied: Yes, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has mentioned you in a very excellent manner. At that time, while delivering the sermon, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: From this door, a man will enter before you (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) From this path, a man will come, who will be extremely blessed, and an angel will have touched his face. (The narrator says) So I praised Allah Almighty for granting me this."
"7200","Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not screen himself from me since my embracing Islam, and whenever he saw me he would receive me with a smile. Once I told him that I could not sit firm on horses. He stroke me on the chest with his hand and said, ""O Allah! Make him firm and make him a guiding and a rightly guided man."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3035)"
"7201","I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I am a person who cannot sit firmly on a horse."" The narrator says: So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed his hand over my chest and said: ""O Allah, make him a guide and a source of guidance."" The narrator says: Until I felt the coolness of his blessed hand."
"7202","I set out with seventy men from my tribe, and we burned it down. I sent a man to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to give him the good news; his kunyah was Abu Arta’ah. He said: O Messenger of Allah! By Allah, I have come to you at a time when I have left that idol-house like a mangy camel. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Allah, bless the horsemen and foot soldiers of the Ahmas tribe."
"7203","I acquire them myself?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “No, rather they are part of your nature.” So Sayyiduna Ashajj (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “All praise is due to Allah alone.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O people of the tribe of ‘Abd al-Qays, what is the reason that I see your faces changed?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, we live in a land that is not suitable for our health. We prepare nabidh (fermented drinks) which help digest the meat in our stomachs, but when we were forbidden from using (nabidh-making) vessels (and we stopped using nabidh), this is now our condition, which is visible on our faces.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Vessels do not make anything lawful or unlawful, but every intoxicant is unlawful. It cannot be that you drink wine, and when you have drunk it well, you confront one another, then someone attacks his cousin and strikes him with a sword, making him lame.” The narrator says: At that time, among those present, there was a lame person with whom this situation had occurred."
"7204","""Indeed there are two traits in you that Allah loves: Forbearance, and deliberateness."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2011)"
"7205","I came to him. He seated me with him on the bed and kept conversing with me. Sayyiduna Wa'il (may Allah be pleased with him) states: At that time, I wished that I had seated him (Muawiyah) in front of me on my mount."
"7206","I am an old, elderly woman, I cannot do any work, please do me a favor, Allah will do you a favor. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Who is your envoy? She replied: ‘Adi bin Hatim. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who has fled from Allah and His Messenger. Then the woman said: Please do me a favor. The woman narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back, at that time a person was present at his side. The woman thinks that he was Sayyiduna ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). That person said: O woman, ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a ride. The woman narrates: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a ride, so he ordered it to be given to me. The woman narrates: Then I came to ‘Adi bin Hatim and I said: You have done such a thing that your father would not have done; you should go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whether you go willingly or out of fear, because so-and-so person went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he obtained such-and-such thing from him. So-and-so person went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he obtained such-and-such thing. (‘Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) says:) I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and at that time there was a woman and some children (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) a child was present in the company of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When it was mentioned that this woman and these children were relatives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I realized that he is not a king like Kisra and Caesar. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O ‘Adi bin Hatim, are you running away from saying that there is no deity except Allah? Is there any deity besides Allah? Are you running away from saying that Allah is the Greatest? Is there anything greater than Allah? The narrator says: So I accepted Islam. I saw the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was very pleased. He said: Indeed, those who incurred [Allah’s] wrath are the Jews, and those who went astray are the Christians."
"7207","The companions of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) were such that it was as if birds were sitting on their heads, while the camels had lowered their necks. The narrator says: I saw, and while I was in this worry, Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) came before me. I asked: Where is the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)? He replied: He is behind me. I was still in this state when it was Abu Musa Ash'ari, I asked: Where is the Messenger of Allah? He said: He is behind me. The narrator named Humaid bin Hilal, with his chain of narration, has transmitted this statement of Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) from Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the voice of Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) behind me, just like the sound of a grinding mill, then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived. I said: O Messenger of Allah! When you are in the enemy's land, you should have a guard. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A person (i.e., an angel) came to me and gave me a choice between two things: either half of my Ummah will enter Paradise, or (through) intercession (countless people will enter Paradise). So I chose intercession. Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you, you know my status, include me among them as well. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You are one of them. Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! You know that we have left our land and families, we believe in Allah and His Messenger, include us among them as well. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Both of you are also among them. The narrator says: We came to the people who had woken up. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A person (i.e., an angel) came to me from my Lord, and he gave me the choice that half of my Ummah would enter Paradise or there would be intercession, so I chose intercession. The attendees said: Include us among them as well. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You people remain silent. They became silent, to the extent that it seemed as if no one wanted to say anything. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This intercession will be for every person who dies in such a state that he does not associate anyone with Allah."
"7208","The girl replied: ""I see a large crowd of people."" Sayyiduna Abu Quhafa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""These must be horsemen."" The lady said: ""I see a man who is coming and going ahead of them."" Sayyiduna Abu Quhafa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O my daughter, he is their overseer, commanding the horses."" Then the girl said: ""By Allah, now the darkness is dispersing."" Sayyiduna Abu Quhafa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""By Allah, now these horses will set off, so quickly take me to my house."" The lady took him down with her, and before they reached the house, they encountered the horsemen. The girl had a necklace made of silver around her neck. A man came before the girl and took the necklace from her neck. The girl narrates: When the Prophet (peace be upon him) entered (Makkah) and came into the mosque, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) brought his father to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him). When the Prophet (peace be upon him) saw him, he said: ""Why did you not leave this noble elder in his house so that I could have come to him myself?"" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted: ""O Messenger of Allah! He is more deserving to come to you than for you to go to him."" The narrator says: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) seated Sayyiduna Abu Quhafa (may Allah be pleased with him) in front of the Prophet (peace be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) passed his hand over his chest and said to him: ""Accept Islam."" So he accepted Islam. The girl narrates: Then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) brought him to the Prophet (peace be upon him) again, and at that time Sayyiduna Abu Quhafa's (may Allah be pleased with him) head was as white as the white flower called thaghama. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Change the color of his hair."" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up, took his sister's hand, and said: ""I ask by Allah and Islam, who has my sister's necklace?"" No one replied. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O my sister, hope for reward regarding your necklace. By Allah, today there is little trustworthiness among people."
"7209","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: What are they? He submitted: My daughter is among the beautiful and attractive women of the Arabs, Umm Habibah; I wish to marry her to you. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Alright. Abu Sufyan submitted: Appoint Muawiyah as your confidant. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Alright. Abu Sufyan submitted: Command me to fight against the polytheists, just as previously I fought against the Muslims. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Alright."
"7210","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""O Allah, grant Muawiyah knowledge of the Book (i.e., the Noble Qur'an) and calculation, and protect him from punishment."
"7211","said: ""It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said: 'The daughter of a Jew' so she wept. Then the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while she was crying, so he said: 'What makes you cry?' She said: 'Hafsah said to me that I am the daughter of a Jew.' So the Prophet ﷺ said: 'And you are the daughter of a Prophet, and your uncle is a Prophet, and you are married to a Prophet, so what is she boasting to you about?' Then he said: 'Fear Allah, O Hafsah.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3894)"
"7212","The people came out (of the fort) with their mattocks, shovels, and baskets. They said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and his army have arrived. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allahu Akbar! Khaybar is destroyed. When we descend into the field of a people, then the condition of those who were warned becomes bad. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) fought with them and defeated them. When the spoils of war were distributed, it was submitted to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): A beautiful and attractive slave woman has come in the share of Sayyiduna Dihyah Kalbi (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) bought her in exchange for seven slaves (or slave women). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entrusted this woman to Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) so that she could prepare her. Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) used to participate in the battles with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called for a dining cloth, it was presented, the cloth was spread, then dates and ghee were brought, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had hais prepared for all of them. The people ate it until they were full. The people asked each other: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) marry this woman or make her an umm walad? Others replied: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made her observe the veil, so she will be his wife. If he had not made her observe the veil, then she would have been considered an umm walad. When Sayyidah Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) was about to mount the ride, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made her observe the veil until she sat behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on the camel. Then when they approached Madinah Munawwarah, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) quickened his mount, and the people also quickened their mounts. The women began to look out. The she-camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stumbled, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyidah Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) fell down. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and made the woman observe the veil. The women said: May Allah keep this Jewish woman away. They spoke ill of Sayyidah Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her). Thabit narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): O Abu Hamzah! Did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) fall from his mount? He replied: Yes, by Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) fell from his mount, O Abu Muhammad!"
"7213","""The Prophet stayed between Khaibar and Al-Madinah for three days when he consummated his marriage to Safiyyah bint Huyayy, and I invited the Muslims to his Walimah, in which there was no bread or meat. He commanded that a leather cloth (be spread) and dates, cottage cheese and ghee were placed on it, and that was his Walimah. The Muslims said: '(Will she be) one of the Mothers of the Believers, or a female slave whom his right hand possesses?' They said: 'If he has a Hijab for her, then she will be one of the Mothers of the Believers and if she does not have a Hijab then she will be a female slave whom his right hand possesses.' When he rode on, he set aside a plate for her behind him and extended a Hijab between her and the people."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3382)"
"7214","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the prophets, 'I' am your share, and among the communities, 'you' are my share."
"7215","When Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, intends to show mercy to an Umma from amongst His servants He calls back His Apostle to his eternal home and makes him a harbinger and recompense in the world to come; and when He intends to cause destruction to an Umma, He punishes it while its Apostle is alive and He destroys it as he (the Apostle) witnesses it and he cools his eyes by destruction as they had belied him and disobeyed his command. (Using translation from Muslim 2288)"
"7216","that about Allah's saying: Thus we have made you a Wasata nation (2:143) - the Prophet ﷺ said: ""The meaning of Wasata is just."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2961)"
"7217","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Your period (i.e. the Muslims' period) in comparison to the periods of the previous nations, is like the period between the ʿAsr prayer and sunset. And your example in comparison to the Jews and the Christians is like the example of a person who employed some laborers and asked them, 'Who will work for me till midday for one Qirat each?' The Jews worked for half a day for one Qirat each. The person asked, 'Who will do the work for me from midday to the time of the ʿAsr (prayer) for one Qirat each?' The Christians worked from midday till the ʿAsr prayer for one Qirat. Then the person asked, 'Who will do the work for me from the ʿAsr till sunset for two Qirats each?' "" The Prophet ﷺ added, ""It is you (i.e. Muslims) who are doing the work from the ʿAsr till sunset, so you will have a double reward. The Jews and the Christians got angry and said, 'We have done more work but got less wages.' Allah said, 'Have I been unjust to you as regards your rights?' They said, 'No.' So Allah said, 'Then it is My Blessing which I bestow on whomever I like. "" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3459)"
"7218","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""The example of the Muslims, Jews, and Christians is like that of a man who hired some people as laborers to work for him all day until night, and he would give them their wages for working until night. They worked for him until midday, then those laborers said: 'We have no need for the wages you have set for us, and the work we have done is wasted.' So that man said"
"7219","Allah has forgiven for me my nation their mistakes and forgetfulness, and what they are forced to do."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2043)"
"7220","""When Allah revealed this Ayah: 'Say: He has the power to send torment on you from above or from under your feet...' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'I seek refuge in Your Face.' So when (the following) was revealed: 'Or to cover you in confusion in party strife, and make you taste the violence of one another (6:65).' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'This is less burdensome' or 'This is easier.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3065)"
"7221","The duration of your existence compared to those who came before you is like the time between the Asr prayer and sunset. The people of the Torah were given the Torah, and they acted upon it until half the day had passed, then they became weary regarding it, so each of them was given one qirat. The people of the Gospel were given the Gospel, and they acted upon it until they reached the time of Asr, then they became weary and each of them was given one qirat. You were given the Qur'an, and you acted upon it until the sun set, so you were given two qirats each. The people of the Torah and the people of the Gospel said: O our Lord! These people did less work than us, yet they received more reward. Allah the Exalted said: Did I wrong you in regard to your reward? They replied: No. So the Lord said: This is My grace, I bestow it upon whom I will."
"7222","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, 'Which of the people are best?' He said: 'My generation, then those that follow them, then those that follow them. Then there will come people whose testimony precedes their oath and whose oath precedes their testimony.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2362)"
"7223","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, 'Which of the people are best?' He said: 'My generation, then those that follow them, then those that follow them. Then there will come people whose testimony precedes their oath and whose oath precedes their testimony.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2362)"
"7224","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: They are the most virtuous people in our view. So he said: The angels who participated in it have the same status among us. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: This narration has been transmitted by Jarir bin Abdul Hameed from Yahya bin Sa’eed from Mu’adh bin Rifaa’ah from his father. Both his father and his grandfather had the honor of participating in the Pledge of Aqabah. He narrates: Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Sufyan Thawri has narrated this narration from Yahya bin Sa’eed from ‘Abayah bin Rifaa’ah and from his grandfather Sayyiduna Rafi’ bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him). Sufyan, compared to Jarir, is a greater memorizer of hadith, more precise, and a greater jurist, and when he remembers something, he does not care who has narrated words contrary to him.)"
"7225","The people ate them until only one pit remained. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do you know what this is? The people replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The good people will depart one by one, until only those like this (useless ones) will remain among you."
"7226","The example of my Ummah is like that of rain; it cannot be determined whether its first part is better or its last part is better."
